## Thing references:  one thing by its type and its name, or its place
-- epic `drawable-thing` P19:  `tableau T1` is the tableau named T1;  `the first tableau` the first one made.

a pile is a list of things
a pile has a name as text
a tableau is a pile
a foundation is a pile
a discard-pile is a pile

// two tableaus named T1:  a reference to T1 below warns, and finds the first
set first-t1 to a new tableau with name = "T1"
set second-t1 to a new tableau with name = "T1"
set t2 to a new tableau with name = "T2"

// foundations, each its own name:  no warning
get a new foundation with name = "clubs"
get a new foundation with name = "hearts"

// two discard piles named "spare", but nothing names one by its name:  no warning
set spare to a new discard-pile with name = "spare"
set other-spare to a new discard-pile with name = "spare"

// names worked out as the program runs are never counted
for each number from 3 to 4
	get a new tableau with name = ("T" + the number)

## by name
print the name of tableau T1
print the name of tableau T2
print the name of foundation "hearts"
// a tableau is a pile:  `pile T2` finds it
print the name of pile T2

## by place
print the name of the first tableau
print the name of the second foundation
print the name of the last tableau
